LβT2 NOT TREATED- EXP1 (JZ_16), EXP2 (JZ_17), EXP3 (JZ_18)
LβT2 TRETATED 10NM (GNRH) - EXP1 (JZ_25), EXP2 (JZ_26), EXP3 (JZ_27)


EXPERIMENTAL SETUP-
1) LβT2 cells were maintained in monolayer culture in DMEM medium (high glucose, GlutaMAX™; Gibco), 10% FBS (EURx) and 1%  penicillin-streptomycin (Gibco). 
2) Cells were split 1:3-1:4 once they achieved 80% confluence. 
3) For gonadotropin releasing hormone (GnRH, Bachem) stimulation experiments, cells were plated in at a density of 5,0 x 10^5 per well. 
4) For the stimulation, the DMEM medium (high glucose with GlutaMAX™) was supplemented with 10% charcoal-stripped FBS (CS-FBS) (Gibco), 1% penicillin-streptomycin , and the stimulant - 10 nM GnRH. GnRH was added in five pulses, each 5-min long, in 2h intervals. 
5) After each pulse, the medium was changed to the intra-pulsatile medium, i.e. DMEM with CS-FBS, but deprived of GnRH. 
6) After the last pulse cells were cultured for 12h in intra-pulsatile medium containing 60 mM KCl. The cells were harvested with Trizol reagent and stored at −80°C before further molecular analyses. 
7) Stimulation experiments were based on Ruf-Zamojski, et al., 2019.

